{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see","id":1236774,"title":"What new Lineages would you like to see?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-19T07:46:21-07:00","id":1236774,"title":"What new Lineages would you like to see?","content":"For me, things are clearly missing from Taoist Alchemy and Aztec Alchemy.<br /> <br /> Moreover some Buddhist legend can be easily adapted as a Chir Batti, the same can be done with Zahhak's lineage in Zoroastrianism.<br /> <br /> The Shinto Tsukumogami would be a good alternative to the Unfleshed.<br /> <br /> It also seems to me that the Inca Mummies are well-suited since they usually appeared from the sacrifice of a noble child and ritualistic form during times of calamity so that the community had someone who spoke directly to the Gods on their behalf and was heard.<br /> <br /> The Return of the Amirani and Hollow would be good.<br /> <br /> Finally something like the Replicants of Blade Runner.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","user":"Ben Linus","date":". 07-19-2018, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T00:28:53-07:00","id":1237049,"title":"","content":"Pinocchio. Maybe Carlo Collodi was to the Lineage what Mary Shelley, Polidori etc was to the Frankensteins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T06:40:48-07:00","id":1237122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237049#post1237049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pinocchio. Maybe Carlo Collodi was to the Lineage what Mary Shelley, Polidori etc was to the Frankensteins.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to get off my butt and write my Geppetto Lineage at some point. I\u2019ve had the idea since early in first edition, but I\u2019ve never gotten around to completing them. My mental image of them is so creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T07:37:48-07:00","id":1237137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237122#post1237122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really need to get off my butt and write my Geppetto Lineage at some point. I\u2019ve had the idea since early in first edition, but I\u2019ve never gotten around to completing them. My mental image of them is so creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creepy is good. Promethean is quickly jumping up the Weirdness and Creepy scales, from what we\u2019ve seen with tidbits of what will be in NH The Tormented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T10:14:03-07:00","id":1237185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237137#post1237137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Creepy is good. Promethean is quickly jumping up the Weirdness and Creepy scales, from what we\u2019ve seen with tidbits of what will be in NH The Tormented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It\u2019s why it\u2019s kind of surprising that I\u2019ve waited so long to write them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T11:07:04-07:00","id":1237203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237185#post1237185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. It\u2019s why it\u2019s kind of surprising that I\u2019ve waited so long to write them up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Lineage I wanted to exist for a really long time as well, so color me curious<br /> <br /> My own ideas were a mess of butchered points to connect with to the Fae or using all the actual esoterical symbolism hidden in the tale to do stuff. But, as I said, it was a mess from which nothing actually came out.<br /> <br /> Looking forward towards what you have in mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-20-2018, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T11:24:18-07:00","id":1237210,"title":"","content":"Some ideas of Lineages that I'm trying to write for a long time:<br /> <br /> - A vegetal oriented one, in the tradition of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rappaccini%27s_Daughter\" target=\"_blank\">Rappacini's Daughter</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alraune\" target=\"_blank\">Alraune</a> - or even Poison Ivy, in a way. Pyros would be the flames that cling to the biblical Burning Bush (or buddhist Lotus Flower) that grows within them, animating their bodies and making them the source of all those legends about Mandragoras being more human than plant.<br /> <br /> - A skeletal Lineage based on the legend or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sedna_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">Sedna</a>.<br /> <br /> - A Zombie Lineage, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 07-20-2018, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T11:55:16-07:00","id":1237219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237210#post1237210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some ideas of Lineages that I'm trying to write for a long time:<br /> <br /> - A vegetal oriented one, in the tradition of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rappaccini%27s_Daughter\" target=\"_blank\">Rappacini's Daughter</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alraune\" target=\"_blank\">Alraune</a> - or even Poison Ivy, in a way. Pyros would be the flames that cling to the biblical Burning Bush (or buddhist Lotus Tree) that grows within them, animating their bodies and making them the source of all those legends about Mandragoras being more human than plant.<br /> <br /> - A skeletal Lineage based on the legend or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sedna_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">Sedna</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I liked the Ideas. And that takes the Buddhist lineage, which responds to the Indian / Japanese source that I miss.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T14:05:01-07:00","id":1237256,"title":"","content":"2nding (or 3rding?) on the Plant Lineage one.<br /> <br /> The only issue I have with Skeletons and Zombies is that Prometheans are <i>already</i> made from corpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:02:41-07:00","id":1237295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237256#post1237256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only issue I have with Skeletons and Zombies is that Prometheans are <i>already</i> made from corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but in my opinion, there's something about the skeletal and zombie-like aspect that's distinct enough from the other corpse-born Lineages. A typical Nepri looks like a dried up mummy, and Tammuz are more clay-like than Romero fresh-from-the-grave risen corpses. For now, there's no Lineages where having your bones laid bare or experimenting putrefaction is truly a defining Disfigurement, and I think there should be, given the weight of such features in the collective imagination when it comes to undead things (almost every fantasy or horror games has its skeletons and/or its zombies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 07-20-2018, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:17:21-07:00","id":1237304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237295#post1237295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, but in my opinion, but there's something about the skeletal and zombie-like aspect that's distinct enough from the other corpse-born Lineages. A typical Nepri looks like a dried up mummy, and Tammuz are more clay-like than Romero fresh-from-the-grave risen corpses. For now, there's no Lineages where having your bones laid bare or experimenting putrefaction is truly a defining Disfigurement, and I think there should be, given the weight of such features in the collective imagination when it comes to undead things (almost every fantasy or horror games has its skeletons and/or its zombies).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Inca Mummies are dehydrated cadavers. Could it serve your concept of &quot;zombie&quot; Adrasalieth?<br /> <br /> I think they match with Prometheans because they are made in times of desperation in the community and literally to negotiate with the Gods on behalf of the community. It seems to me a legitimate motive to extract Pyros and a little ironic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:40:17-07:00","id":1237314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237304#post1237304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Inca Mummies are dehydrated cadavers. Could it serve your concept of &quot;zombie&quot; Adrasalieth?<br /> <br /> I think they match with Prometheans because they are made in times of desperation in the community and literally to negotiate with the Gods on behalf of the community. It seems to me a legitimate motive to extract Pyros and a little ironic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I thought about Mesoamerican Prometheans as being more skeletal than zombie-like (one notable inspiration on this side would be the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tzitzimitl\" target=\"_blank\">Tzitzimitl</a>). Also, the homebrew Lineage I made around Skeletons, the Sedna, need corpses of people chosen by a group as a scapegoat for their Generative Act, which matches with the Mesoamerican traditions of human sacrifice. <br /> <br /> Since the concepts of some Lineages seem to have interested some people, I'm gonna check if I still have the docs at hand and try to post them here this week ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T17:13:54-07:00","id":1237344,"title":"","content":"I don't think you need a Lineage for a skeletal Promethean. What you're doing there is more along the lines of making a Construct (that is, a Promethean that's made of inanimate matter rather than corpses), much like the Unfleshed, except that the construction material is \u201cbones\u201d. To me, what you need to define a Lineage is an Element and a Humour, to provide a thematic basis for its Wasteland, Disquiet, and Torment. <br /> <br /> As for the idea of a plant-based Lineage, I could get behind that; though I'd tend to blend it a bit with the Gepetto/Pinocchio idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T02:49:11-07:00","id":1237444,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11431\" data-vbnamecard=\"11431\">Adrasalieth</a> I second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>: more important than the material is the thematic concept behind the lineage, and so there should be more focus on the Element/Humour behind it.<br /> The restrictions of the Sedna are interesting though. Would like to see that write up, but not nearly as much as your Alraune.<br /> Wood as an Element would work excellently, seeing how it is an element in the Chinese system. What Humour would the 'vegetable' Lineage have? Personally, it made me think of something like Aquatic, being stretched too thin, so that in Torment they become unable to act quickly, and tend to 'grow roots' (sorry) in a place or tend towards superficial, repetitive actions. Curious to see your take on it.<br /> I would totally love a plant-based Promethean lineage, and I like the fluff bit about Mandragoras, the Burning Bush and Lotus flowers a lot, so I am rooting (Sorry!) for you!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:11:21-07:00","id":1237468,"title":"","content":"wouldn't the Pinocchio lineage just be Unfleashed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:52:22-07:00","id":1237481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237444#post1237444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Humour would the 'vegetable' Lineage have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vegetable Oil, obviously. \u263a<br /> <br /> More seriously, how about Sap? Torment might manifest in keeping things close or to themselves, representing stuff getting stuck in sap.<br /> <br /> They would probably gain Pyros by staying in Sunlight. What Bestowments might they have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:54:47-07:00","id":1237483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237481#post1237481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They would probably gain Pyros by staying in Sunlight. What Bestowments might they have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to use photosynthesis to sustain themselves in place of food or drink, being able to &quot;put down roots&quot; and make it more difficult for them to be moved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24149-the-third-king","name":"The Third King","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T07:14:18-07:00","id":1237488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237468#post1237468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wouldn't the Pinocchio lineage just be Unfleashed?</div> </div> </div> </div>My original idea for them predated the introduction of the Unfleshed, but ultimately it didn\u2019t change much. Pinocchio was Unfleshed, and achieved the New Dawn. He would also become the demiurge of the Geppetto Lineage. <br /> For the element, I\u2019ve always considered them to represent wood, and sap was the humor I was going to use. Originally, I\u2019d planned on going with a deficiency of one of the four humors ( melancholic, if I remember correctly), but once other humors started showing up, it made more sense to give them their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T07:42:06-07:00","id":1237500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Third King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237483#post1237483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being able to use photosynthesis to sustain themselves in place of food or drink, being able to &quot;put down roots&quot; and make it more difficult for them to be moved?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure Photosynthesis is all that superior to what Prometheans can do anyways, especially with Acid Stomach. &quot;Rooting&quot; to make them more resistant might work. Bonus to Resistance rolls when not moving? Additional Doors in Social Maneuvering? Armor for bark-like skin?<br /> <br /> What are some other &quot;plant&quot; traits?<br /> <br /> Using Alraune as a source, Heart of Steel or something like it seems fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-21-2018, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T07:48:17-07:00","id":1237503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237500#post1237500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure Photosynthesis is all that superior to what Prometheans can do anyways, especially with Acid Stomach. &quot;Rooting&quot; to make them more resistant might work. Bonus to Resistance rolls when not moving? Additional Doors in Social Maneuvering? Armor for bark-like skin?<br /> <br /> What are some other &quot;plant&quot; traits?<br /> <br /> Using Alraune as a source, Heart of Steel or something like it seems fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regrowth? able to eventually restore missing limbs even if they are destroyed? I can't remember if all lineages have the ability to restore missing limbs by reattachement or if its just frankensteins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T15:52:35-07:00","id":1237605,"title":"","content":"Suggesting something about healing oneself, or others at the expense of oneself as the plant Lineage\u2019s Bestowment. Monstrous plants are sometimes asaociated with being miracle herbs, and the Wood xing/vector/action in Daoism is strongly associated with life (not just the sedentary growth of plants, but birth and expansion and explosive growth.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T15:55:11-07:00","id":1237606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237468#post1237468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wouldn't the Pinocchio lineage just be Unfleshed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's not about what they're made of. Per the \u201cConstructed vs. Unfleshed\u201d box on page 76, <i>any</i> Lineage can be made out of things other than corpses, not just the Unfleshed. <br /> <br /> With the Unfleshed, their Torment drives them to become more robotic in their personality, and/or to become killing machines; their Disquiet causes people to think of them as things rather than as people. That's not Pinocchio, and it's not a \u201cplant Lineage\u201d. <br /> <br /> I think that's the main thing missing here: Torment and Disquiet. Wasteland is generally easy to determine, as it's tied to the Element and usually has a fairly literal effect; but Torment and Disquiet are about thoughts, feelings, motivations, emotion, and so on. Frankensteins tend toward rage as their Torment, and tend to be scapegoated by Disquiet; Galeteids in Torment give into dark passions and inspire unhealthy obsession in others; Osirans become unfeeling, manipulative, and lethargic or megalomaniacal, and trigger deceptiveness in others; Tammuz either become irritable and anxious or depressed and enervated, often losing the ability to speak, and cause others to misunderstand them and each other; the Ulgans feel alienated and cause others to see them as monsters. What are the key personality traits of Gepetto's creations? What happens when a \u201cPlant Promethean\u201d goes into Torment or inflicts Disquiet? \u201cI'm made of vegetation\u201d doesn't say much in these regards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T18:57:08-07:00","id":1237643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237606#post1237606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's the main thing missing here: Torment and Disquiet. Wasteland is generally easy to determine, as it's tied to the Element and usually has a fairly literal effect; but Torment and Disquiet are about thoughts, feelings, motivations, emotion, and so on. Frankensteins tend toward rage as their Torment, and tend to be scapegoated by Disquiet; Galeteids in Torment give into dark passions and inspire unhealthy obsession in others; Osirans become unfeeling, manipulative, and lethargic or megalomaniacal, and trigger deceptiveness in others; Tammuz either become irritable and anxious or depressed and enervated, often losing the ability to speak, and cause others to misunderstand them and each other; the Ulgans feel alienated and cause others to see them as monsters. What are the key personality traits of Gepetto's creations? What happens when a \u201cPlant Promethean\u201d goes into Torment or inflicts Disquiet? \u201cI'm made of vegetation\u201d doesn't say much in these regards.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237481#post1237481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More seriously, how about Sap? Torment might manifest in keeping things close or to themselves, representing stuff getting stuck in sap.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for Disquiet, it might not seem like much variation, but what about it manifesting as people ignoring their very existence. It isn't seeing them as tools so much as &quot;who pays attention to the grass they walk on?&quot; kind of isolation. Yeah, it isn't as violent as the others, but being utterly unpersoned can't be fun (or safe, to a certain degree - it doesn't matter if you run them over, trample them, or shoot/stab them if they are in the way; it's not like they are a <i>person</i> after all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T21:13:31-07:00","id":1237679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237643#post1237643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As for Disquiet, it might not seem like much variation, but what about it manifesting as people ignoring their very existence. It isn't seeing them as tools so much as &quot;who pays attention to the grass they walk on?&quot; kind of isolation. Yeah, it isn't as violent as the others, but being utterly unpersoned can't be fun (or safe, to a certain degree - it doesn't matter if you run them over, trample them, or shoot/stab them if they are in the way; it's not like they are a <i>person</i> after all).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just go back to the original story. The Torment could be the Gepetto starts gaining addictions to drugs, alcohol, and other vices.<br /> <br /> Edit: wait never mind you were talking about the plant lineage..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","user":"Grimmi05","date":". 07-22-2018, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T23:34:19-07:00","id":1238148,"title":"","content":"Other possible humours and/or 'Elements' for Lineages:<br /> Vitae, Mana, Plasm, Sekhem.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like sap as a humour for plant-based Prometheans. (Swampthing!)<br /> The &quot;being ignored&quot; Sounds mostly cool. Seeing them as an unfeeling thing to be harvested also works imo.<br /> What about the wasteland? Everything growing sticky, and covered in Pollen and weeds? Plants growing hard, thorny and poisonous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T06:27:32-07:00","id":1238197,"title":"","content":"I've been kicking around the idea for a food one. Think Gingerbread Man and The Stinky Cheese Man. I blame The Great British Baking Show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T07:09:39-07:00","id":1238212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1238148#post1238148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like sap as a humour for plant-based Prometheans. (Swampthing!)<br /> The &quot;being ignored&quot; Sounds mostly cool. Seeing them as an unfeeling thing to be harvested also works imo.<br /> What about the wasteland? Everything growing sticky, and covered in Pollen and weeds? Plants growing hard, thorny and poisonous?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as Wasteland effects go, I could either see the area become overgrown in invasive, dangerous plants... Or the opposite, with all plant life getting wilted and dying. Wastelands are supposed to be Flux-powered, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T11:43:35-07:00","id":1239003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1238212#post1238212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as Wasteland effects go, I could either see the area become overgrown in invasive, dangerous plants... Or the opposite, with all plant life getting wilted and dying. Wastelands are supposed to be Flux-powered, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Plant life wilting and dying sounds very similar to other Wastelands somehow.<br /> Maybe plants growing EVERYWHERE, due to overloading with Flux? I am talking breaking up asphalt severely, growing on window frames, maybe even on the fur of living animals.<br /> In later stages, you could have plants grow on glass, in oil (goodbye, cars!) etc. Plants quickly die, fall off, and provide a layer for other plants to grow on, who return the cycle.<br /> Sort of a return of the jungle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T15:07:03-07:00","id":1239053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1238148#post1238148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other possible humours and/or 'Elements' for Lineages:<br /> Vitae, Mana, Plasm, Sekhem.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, unless you work a hybrid line created by supernatural beings that has characteristics of the creator (something that almost transformed the Gargoyles into the Classical Worlds of Darkness).<br /> <br /> But I imagine beyond Sap, things like Blood, Salt and sand as interesting things.<br /> <br /> There are legends of animated beings wearing lining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T23:51:21-07:00","id":1239210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1239053#post1239053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, unless you work a hybrid line created by supernatural beings that has characteristics of the creator (something that almost transformed the Gargoyles into the Classical Worlds of Darkness).<br /> <br /> But I imagine beyond Sap, things like Blood, Salt and sand as interesting things.<br /> <br /> There are legends of animated beings wearing lining.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily hybrid. Beings with access to those Materials (among others: hunters, minor splats etc) could well create a promethean. Ulgan have essence, yet are not hybrids.<br /> The Main question would be defining the effects<br /> <br /> <br /> Salt and Sand would be good, though. Sanguine is basically Blood, like melancholic is Black bile.<br /> Bone however could also work. Acid, maybe, seeing how the human body is full of them. <br /> <br /> I adore Salt because you could go a bit Charles Dexter Ward with that, and you know me, I love me some good Lovecraftian references :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 07-27-2018, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T01:53:52-07:00","id":1239227,"title":"","content":"Two of the core Lineages have origin stories revolving around the attempt to resurrect a loved one, but primarily reflect different concepts in their makeup. I think there's room for a Lineage that goes the whole hog on the resurrection angle: a &quot;Morbid Humour,&quot; a Disquiet wherein people see in the Promethean reflections of those they've lost and grow angry when she doesn't live up to their memories, a Torment that's still and dead or else obsessed with a fear of loss. My original idea was a Mesopotamian Lineage with an ambiguous connection to the Tammuz, but that's not really necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T08:10:44-07:00","id":1240438,"title":"","content":"The Andean Lineage I imagine, I think is associated with salt and be seen as lofty beings who have been elevated to a higher condition and therefore the favors they bestow are seen as something within &quot;just their obligation&quot; with people becoming ungrateful for what they is granted (it is becoming increasingly necessary to get affection) and even angry if they do not do a favor they are already accustomed to.<br /> <br /> To reflect its function, powers over the climate would be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:01:13-07:00","id":1240922,"title":"","content":"I would love a lineage that really nails the BOOK version of Frankenstein, maybe lampshading the wretched by their demiurge being twistedly inspired by the story but misunderstanding Victor's process. I know I've seen homunculus lineages on the forums that would be really cool refined into 2e. Picture bodies being dissolved and remolded on a human template, like a cross between FMA human transmutation, old alchemical generation of life and a caterpillar turning into a butterfly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2706-comicjunkie1","name":"comicjunkie1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T22:38:27-07:00","id":1242880,"title":"","content":"Some sort of plastic based mannequin one? Or would that be some type of unfleshed? (Hmmm... maybe there are five unfleshed liniages based on wood, metal, stone, plastic, and ... I'm drawing a blank. Pure thought, maybe? Pinocchio, Taltos, Gollum, Mannequin, and Psyche?)<br /> <br /> I wish I could remember all of the old D&amp;D para-elemental types. Mud, steam, salt, void, ash, radiance, and some others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 08-05-2018, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T02:15:02-07:00","id":1242903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1242880#post1242880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some sort of plastic based mannequin one? Or would that be some type of unfleshed? (Hmmm... maybe there are five unfleshed liniages based on wood, metal, stone, plastic, and ... I'm drawing a blank. Pure thought, maybe? Pinocchio, Taltos, Gollum, Mannequin, and Psyche?)<br /> <br /> I wish I could remember all of the old D&amp;D para-elemental types. Mud, steam, salt, void, ash, radiance, and some others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if primarily Constructs, it could be a separate Lineage if it\u2019s different enough compared to the Unfleshed. And plastic sounds pretty interesting...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T06:26:45-07:00","id":1243191,"title":"","content":"I've been kicking around the idea of a historical and now gone lineage based around the idea of the Tower of Babel and The Great Flood. I always liked the translation of Gilgamesh where the gods sent a flood to wipe out Humanity because they were too loud. Switching that over to Promethean, what if there was a lineage based around the element of Air and language whose Disquiet lead to communication breaking down and very loud Wastelands forming? Then the Great Flood could actually have been a Firestorm wiping out that Lineage. And that's where the stories of the Tower of Babel and The Great Flood come from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T06:34:09-07:00","id":1243193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237210#post1237210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some ideas of Lineages that I'm trying to write for a long time:<br /> <br /> <br /> - A skeletal Lineage based on the legend or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sedna_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">Sedna</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Speak more<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T14:53:15-07:00","id":1243300,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that in East Asia, there may be five entirely different primary Lineages based instead on the Taoist elements of Earth, Wood, Metal, Fire and Water, and Ying/Yang alchemy. Not sure what their Refinements would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 08-06-2018, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T15:36:07-07:00","id":1243314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1243300#post1243300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that in East Asia, there may be five entirely different primary Lineages based instead on the Taoist elements of Earth, Wood, Metal, Fire and Water, and Ying/Yang alchemy. Not sure what their Refinements would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d keep the five base Refinements the same (though they can be called other things). But some differented complex refinements seem possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-17-2018, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T16:10:56-07:00","id":1243320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1243314#post1243314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019d keep the five base lineages the same (though they can be called other things). But some differented complex refinements seem possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would give to exchange Ectoplasm for Wood.<br /> <br /> Metal refinements remain a thing of Taoism. But although all the important elements here are there, the same does not happen with all the elements there. Arsenic for example is very important to them.<br /> <br /> The breeding of lineages may differ a bit too.<br /> <br /> <br /> A mechanic of Yin and Yang would make sense to apply.<br /> <br /> A Promethean the East Linages is a book I would buy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T16:23:32-07:00","id":1243324,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry, I meant five base REFINEMENTS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T22:28:35-07:00","id":1243407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1243324#post1243324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, sorry, I meant five base REFINEMENTS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Observing people, retreating to comtemplate, perfecting the body, studying your condition and fuck everything are logically universal approaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T23:59:33-08:00","id":1268190,"title":"","content":"I distinctly remember that Dataweaver once posted a Lineage that was based around disease and chemical contamination, a sort of \u201c safer\u201d Zeka. That would be interesting to see done.<br /> <br /> Though of course I might be remembering two separate Lineages-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T07:45:53-08:00","id":1268268,"title":"","content":"It was two separate Lineages, based on the old designation of Weapons of Mass Destruction and the military equivalent of the Hazmat Suit (at the time I first came up with this it was called an \u201cNBC Suit\u201d, where \u201cNBC\u201d stood for \u201cNuclear, Biological, Chemical\u201d). <br /> <br /> Together with the Nuclear Prometheans, the Chemical/Toxic and Biological/Plague Prometheans were supposed to form a trio of \u201cHazmat\u201d Lineages that were defined by contamination by dangerous materials: the Toxic Prometheans specialized in poisons and drugs, while the Plague Prometheans were all about infectious diseases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T11:46:55-08:00","id":1268356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1268268#post1268268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was two separate Lineages, based on the old designation of Weapons of Mass Destruction and the military equivalent of the Hazmat Suit (at the time I first came up with this it was called an \u201cNBC Suit\u201d, where \u201cNBC\u201d stood for \u201cNuclear, Biological, Chemical\u201d).<br /> <br /> Together with the Nuclear Prometheans, the Chemical/Toxic and Biological/Plague Prometheans were supposed to form a trio of \u201cHazmat\u201d Lineages that were defined by contamination by dangerous materials: the Toxic Prometheans specialized in poisons and drugs, while the Plague Prometheans were all about infectious diseases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this plays into something that occurred to me a while back - the 2e core mentions a World War I Lineage known as the Faceless, who were created from those killed by chemical weapons, and one of the Promethean eras in Dark Eras 2 is World War I, so we might see them in DE2. (Although perhaps not as focused on toxicity as Dataweaver's suggestion.).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T13:22:29-08:00","id":1268388,"title":"","content":"I wanna see Clones as a lineage, if only to satiate my need to better populate my Infinite Macabre homebrew.<br /> <br /> ...And maybe a weird, Guyver-esque Lineage, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T22:37:56-08:00","id":1268485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1268388#post1268388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...And maybe a weird, Guyver-esque Lineage, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>*eyes wander towards Deviant*<br /> <br /> ...don't want to wait?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T09:47:12-08:00","id":1268572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1268485#post1268485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *eyes wander towards Deviant*<br /> <br /> ...don't want to wait?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a feature in Deviant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T09:56:54-08:00","id":1268574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1268572#post1268572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that a feature in Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>DaveB's cited Guyver as Deviant source material.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T11:19:03-08:00","id":1268587,"title":"","content":"Oh... sweet. Then I just need a Clone lineage, or failing that, advice on how to homebrew one. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T11:47:57-08:00","id":1269303,"title":"","content":"If we have a clone lineage, another lineage of prometheans that do not immediately wake up but are born as unconscious constructs that later become aware (as in Westwolrd) would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T13:24:00-08:00","id":1269329,"title":"","content":"Clone lineages are cool, but lineages created by supernatural creatures are really cool too. While Extempore seem to have been expanded to include such anomalies , I would love to see Prometheans descended from such oddities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T15:36:35-08:00","id":1269377,"title":"","content":"Going on the path of the Crossover some kind of being that is created by other supernatural beings using the exercise of these beings would be cool (something like the Gargoyles of the Classic World of Darkness). One can argue that Extempore already covers these beings, but I do not know, it seems to me something different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T13:28:37-08:00","id":1269895,"title":"","content":"Consider this a teaser for something I\u2019m working on later in the week: Gravetallow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T12:34:37-08:00","id":1272672,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering of a Stolen Devine Lineage.<br /> <br /> Though the years mankind has always sought to be closer to what is holy. Sometimes they succeed and become something else - a Saint, a Guru, a Bhodivista. Sometimes they breach the vault of Heaven for but a brief moment and in yearning for the Divine drag back the quintessence of something holy back to the base fallen Earth. On Christmass Eve, the prayers of a faithful congregation cause the Christ Child to come alive. A monk worshipping the Holy Host in Monstrance finds himself before the living figure of his Savior. An astrophysicist gases through his telescope marvelling at the wonders of Creation. In a flash, he obtains a breakthrough on the nature of the Cosmos and finds that his telescope is now an alive girl, a manifestation of the goddess Sophia in the beauty of her wisdom. A Sleepwalker accompanies his Mage friend through the seven Heavens and captures some Celestial fire in a jar, only for the fire to take human form on Earth.<br /> <br /> Element: Celestial Fire.<br /> Humour: Sacred<br /> <br /> Refinements: Wings of Fire / having a halo over your head shedding holy light, blessing holy water and salt, Adamic knowledge of the names of all things, perfect sense of time and the weather, a talent for prophecy, intuitive knowledge of complex mathematics/astrophysics/cosmology,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T05:06:08-08:00","id":1272958,"title":"","content":"One idea that occurs to me is a Lineage of Prometheans created by children for childish reasons. Essentially dolls, stuffed animals, and imaginary friends that are made to strike back against childhood fears. Overprotective guardians who don't know what to do when their charges outgrow them. Their torment would make them view the world in false dichotomies (good, bad, love, hate, etc.) and their Disquiet would trigger overprotectiveness and suspicion (often revolving around fears of mental stability).<br /> <br /> For clone lineages there is a lot of potential to be found in the NeoSapiens from Exosquad. Some of their known issues (e.g. difficulty with abstract thought and a potential genetic disease that causes them to slowly melt) make a lot of sense as Promethean Torments or conditions. They do overlap somewhat with Golems in that they were created as servants for hostile environments, but they are consistently shown to be willing to fight back They also do a lot of genetic engineering on themselves, which with a little tweaking would map very well to alchemy.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I wouldn't steal the NeoSapiens whole cloth, but they are a rich vein of source material to mine.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T15:27:46-08:00","id":1273022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1272958#post1272958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea that occurs to me is a Lineage of Prometheans created by children for childish reasons. Essentially dolls, stuffed animals, and imaginary friends that are made to strike back against childhood fears. Overprotective guardians who don't know what to do when their charges outgrow them. Their torment would make them view the world in false dichotomies (good, bad, love, hate, etc.) and their Disquiet would trigger overprotectiveness and suspicion (often revolving around fears of mental stability).<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It would be interesting for them to be an absolutely trustworthy and protective force for the child and only develop the torment when the child grows up in that case. Which will not take that long.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T06:00:06-08:00","id":1273082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1273022#post1273022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be interesting for them to be an absolutely trustworthy and protective force for the child and only develop the torment when the child grows up in that case. Which will not take that long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or when separated from the child. One possible bestowment is that they could hide themselves as an inanimate object, basically a &quot;safe&quot; looking version of their real form, like a worn down stuffed toy or a slightly broken doll. It makes it so that they can stay close to their charges, but it doesn't stop the spread of their disquiet. Parents, guardians, and teachers are going to start looking at the doll with suspicion and taking it away because &quot;It's not good for a child to be so attached...&quot; or some other reason. Then their torment can flare until they manage to work their way back to the child.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T09:07:28-07:00","id":1390794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1237122#post1237122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really need to get off my butt and write my Geppetto Lineage at some point. I\u2019ve had the idea since early in first edition, but I\u2019ve never gotten around to completing them. My mental image of them is so creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Years late, but this comes to mind: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=nM2Wz6NdPZs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=nM2Wz6NdPZs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=nM2Wz6NdPZs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=nM2Wz6NdPZs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T22:22:29-07:00","id":1391130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"