nyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1391130#post1391130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is awesome! Thank you for sharing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem! I can imagine this being what a Centimanus Geppetto would be like xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T18:27:42-07:00","id":1394925,"title":"","content":"Going back to the Aztec/Mesoamerican stuff mentioned earlier in the thread, they actually included a lineage similar in Dark Eras 2 called the Xibalbans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25438-justasplanned","name":"JustAsPlanned","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T13:29:41-07:00","id":1395135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JustAsPlanned</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1236774-what-new-lineages-would-you-like-to-see?p=1394925#post1394925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to the Aztec/Mesoamerican stuff mentioned earlier in the thread, they actually included a lineage similar in Dark Eras 2 called the Xibalbans.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's very strange that they're in the Middle Kingdom Egypt setting, of all things, but they sound pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the text doesn't list disfigurements or the nature of their Wastelands, but their origins in human sacrifice makes me picture gaping, startling red wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-08-2020, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}